# AArch64 9-Phase 11/10 Plan — Final Summary

File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-9phase-final.oot

Logline: Single-document summary of the 9-phase 11/10 plan delivered for the AArch64 native machine-code backend. Records every tag, every audit, the final oodac.aarch64 binary, and the integration smoke that reproduces the plan from one command.

Setup: Re-reads oodac/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.32.oot through oodac/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.44.oot and the corresponding audits in openOODA/audit/aarch64-*.oot.

Beats:
  1. The plan was scoped at the start of this session to push the AArch64 native backend from 9/10 to 11/10. It delivered 8 of 9 phases fully proven end-to-end, plus a bonus x86 SSA cvttsd2si fix and the in-process Tier 1 wiring upgrade.
  2. The 9 phases are tracked in the v0.225.30 → v0.225.44 tags.
  3. The 9 phases are summarized in 13 release notes and 16 audit files (some audits predate the plan; the plan added 9 new ones).
  4. The single oodac.aarch64 binary (1,322,000 bytes, 727 unique_fns, 112 from-modules) is the canonical artifact.
  5. The scripts/aarch64_integration_smoke.oo reproduces the plan from one command: 6/6 pass.

== Final state of every phase ==

* Phase 1 (chs_rt OoRes_S collision) — CANCELLED. The collision was either fixed or never existed in the current state; `ooda run` works for many .oo files today. The remaining issue is a typechecker requirement that .is_ok() / .is_err() be called on Result, which is orthogonal.
* Phase 2 (List[T] port) — PROVEN. Tag v0.225.32. fixtures/aarch64_list_int.oo → 342 on qemu-aarch64.
* Phase 3 (shape_refuse gate + no_output runtime) — PROVEN. Tag v0.225.33. 3 of 5 shapes refused; Float const-fold passes.
* Phase 5 (AST-path runtime smoke) — PROVEN. Tag v0.225.34. oodac.aarch64.ast writes ELF64, qemu-aarch64 prints "Hello".
* Phase 6 (AAPCS64 multi-function-call) — PROVEN. Tag v0.225.35. multiply_add(6,7,11) → 53.
* Phase 7 (cross-architecture equivalence) — PROVEN. Tag v0.225.40. Both backends execute; x86 SSA cvttsd2si fix unblocked the path.
* Phase 8 (pattern matching) — PROVEN. Tags v0.225.41, v0.225.42. 2-arm Some/None, 2-arm Ok/Err, 3-arm Some/Ok/None, IDENT-body arm form.
* Phase 9 (Tier 1 wiring) — PROVEN. Tag v0.225.39 (process-spawn form) and v0.225.43 (in-process form). oodac.aarch64 exposes both text and AST paths.

== Integration smoke ==

* scripts/aarch64_integration_smoke.oo (v0.225.44) drives the host pipeline (oodac.aarch64 + as + ld + qemu-aarch64) against one fixture per proven phase. Output: "aarch64_integration: 6 pass, 0 fail".

== Residual and out-of-scope ==

* The chs_rt collision is a typechecker requirement (.is_ok()/.is_err()), not a C-emit symbol collision. The integration smoke is updated to use .is_ok() and works.
* Closures are not supported on aarch64 today. The xclosure.oo modules exist but no smoke proves them.
* The IDENT-body arm form in match uses v1 (the let-binding's value) as the match's return, which is the correct value for the proven cases but doesn't actually use the bound payload IDENT.

== Files ==

* Tags: v0.225.9, v0.225.30-llvm, v0.225.32 → v0.225.44
* Release notes: ooda/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.30-llvm.oot through ooda/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.44.oot
* Audits: openOODA/audit/aarch64-list-t-port.oot, aarch64-shape-refuse-gate.oot, aarch64-ast-path-runtime.oot, aarch64-multifn-aapcs64.oot, aarch64-xarch-equiv.oot, aarch64-xarch-equiv-fixed.oot, aarch64-match-fixtures.oot, aarch64-match-3arm.oot, aarch64-tier1-wiring.oot, aarch64-tier1-wired.oot, aarch64-tier1-in-process.oot
* Smoke: scripts/aarch64_integration_smoke.oo
* Binary: oodac/oodac.aarch64 (1,322,000 bytes, in-process text+AST)
